THIRD-PARTY DATA
----------------

This software contains no third-party data. It reads two public sources at
runtime, and the terms of each stay with the source, not with this licence:

  numbeo.com   Cost-of-living figures are Numbeo's proprietary data, read from
               public web pages for personal and research use. This project
               redistributes no dataset and ships no scraped values. Cite
               Numbeo when you publish a figure obtained through this tool, and
               do not commit its output to a public repository.
               robots.txt (checked 2026-08-25) disallows only
               /heavy_crawling.any. This client is single-threaded per host,
               paces itself, caches aggressively, and never retries a 429.

  nomads.com   Read through the MCP endpoint at https://nomads.com/mcp, which
               states in its own handshake that results are capped and rate
               limited and that it is not a bulk data source. This client
               honours that: one call per invocation, no pagination loop, and
               the server's own attribution string is carried through to
               output.

If you are building something commercial on cost-of-living data, buy Numbeo's
Data API licence. This tool exists so that a person comparing a handful of
cities does not have to.
